patch-manager for Debian
------------------------

Upstream installs the program as 'patman' and its documentation uses that
name throughout. Debian already has an unrelated program called 'patman'
(the PatMaN short-sequence aligner, in the patman package), so this package
installs it only as 'patch-manager', the upstream alternative name.

To use the upstream name, add an alias to your shell configuration:

  alias patman=patch-manager

 -- Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0600
